new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c791f3e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_filepanel.m
@@ -0,0 +1,645 @@
+/*
+ * FineWine: the Mac's own open and save panels for the Windows file dialogs.
+ *
+ * A Windows program that asks for a file or a folder gets Wine's own dialog, which shows the
+ * Mac's disk as drive Z: and knows nothing of the Finder's sidebar, of iCloud, of tags or of
+ * search. comdlg32 asks here first (see dlls/comdlg32/macpanel.c): this shows an NSOpenPanel
+ * or NSSavePanel for the request and hands back the Unix paths that were chosen, which
+ * comdlg32 turns into Windows paths.
+ *
+ * The panel runs as a modal one on the main thread, which is how a Mac program shows it: it
+ * stays in front of the program's windows and they take no clicks while it is open. Wine's
+ * own work on the main thread goes on meanwhile, since the driver's requests are served in
+ * the modal run loop mode as well. The Windows thread that asked does not wait in here: it
+ * gets a number for the panel at once and asks again for the result (macdrv_file_panel_poll)
+ * while it keeps handling its window messages.
+ *
